# Source-Scoped Question Commit and ASR Latency

Status: NOT_STARTED
Milestone: A2 Fast finalization
Dependencies: 28_QUESTION_DRAFTS.todo

## Purpose

Finalize the intended Mic question without waiting for silence or stopping Computer transcription.

## Tasks

- [ ] Negotiate v3/commit capability while preserving strict v1/v2 behavior.
- [ ] Add typed commit envelopes to the single ordered sender queue under the audio watermark lock.
- [ ] Define question start/end boundaries, device-buffer lag and delivered-versus-spoken sample semantics.
- [ ] Track processed sample watermarks server-side; do not use received bytes as decoded coverage.
- [ ] Flush/recreate only the selected decoder with cumulative offsets/global IDs preserved.
- [ ] Ack source/epoch/watermark/final reference; deduplicate retries by session/source/request ID.
- [ ] Reject stale/changed duplicate controls and keep Computer capture/decoder state continuous.
- [ ] Keep explicit send-as-shown separate; timeout must not silently send another draft.
- [ ] Measure paced dual-source commit/fidelity p50/p95 before tuning capture chunk size.
- [ ] Evaluate bounded question-only Whisper refinement without changing already-sent text.

## Acceptance criteria

- [ ] No clipped/duplicated final words, old-question leakage or cross-source reset in the synthetic matrix.
- [ ] Empty/repeated commits are acknowledged without duplicate finals or new IDs.
- [ ] Commit and snapshot latency targets are measured, not inferred from batch RTF or stream-start timing.
- [ ] Whisper or lower-buffer changes are promoted only with actual live-path quality/latency evidence.

## Completion evidence

- None. Pinned Vosk FinalResult/replacement feasibility is researched, not implemented.

## Completion log

- 2026-10-08 - Planned; local ASR remains default and global Stop is not the question boundary.
